==Reception==

Season eight received critical acclaim and won multiple awards, including two [[Emmy Award]]s: "[[Homer's Phobia]]" won for [[Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Animated Program (for Programming Less Than One Hour)|Outstanding Animated Program (for Programming One Hour or Less)]] in 1997,<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=http://www.infoplease.com/ipa/A0151479.html |title=1996–1997 Emmy Awards |access-date=2005-02-13 |publisher=infoplease.com}}</ref> and [[Alf Clausen]] and [[Ken Keeler]] won for "Outstanding Individual Achievement in Music and Lyrics" with the song "We Put the Spring in Springfield" from the episode "[[Bart After Dark]]".<ref name="Keeler">{{cite video |people=Keeler, Ken |date=2005 |title=The Simpsons The Complete Eighth Season DVD commentary for the episode "Bart After Dark" |medium=DVD |publisher=20th Century Fox}}</ref> Clausen also received an Emmy nomination for "Outstanding Music Direction" for "[[Simpsoncalifragilisticexpiala(Annoyed Grunt)cious]]".<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=http://theenvelope.latimes.com/factsheets/awardsdb/env-awards-db-search,0,7169155.htmlstory?searchtype=person&query=Alf+Clausen |title=Every show, every winner, every nominee |access-date=2005-02-10 |publisher=The Envelope}}</ref> "[[Brother from Another Series]]" was nominated for the Emmy for "Sound Mixing For a Comedy Series or a Special".<ref>[[Associated Press]], "49th Annual Primetime Emmy Nominations", ''[[The Globe and Mail]]'', July 25, 1997, pg. C.9.</ref> For "Homer's Phobia", [[Mike B. Anderson|Mike Anderson]] won the Annie Award for Best Individual Achievement: Directing in a TV Production, and the WAC Winner Best Director for Primetime Series at the 1998 World Animation Celebration.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=http://www.awn.com/mag/issue2.12/2.12pages/2.12wacintro.html |title=The World Animation Celebration: Pasadena's Festival |access-date=2005-05-13 |publisher=Animation World Magazine |last=Kenyon |first=Heather}}</ref> [[GLAAD|Gay & Lesbian Alliance Against Defamation]] awarded the episode the [[GLAAD Media Award]] for "Outstanding TV&nbsp;– Individual Episode".<ref>{{cite book |editor-last=Alberti |editor-first=John  |year=2005 |title=Leaving Springfield: 'The Simpsons' and the Possibility of Oppositional Culture |publisher=Wayne State University Press |isbn=0-8143-2849-0 |page=[https://archive.org/details/leavingspringfie00albe/page/241 241] |url-access=registration |url=https://archive.org/details/leavingspringfie00albe/page/241 }}</ref>  On Rotten Tomatoes, the eighth season of ''The Simpsons'' has a 100% approval rating based on 7 critical  reviews.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web| url=https://www.rottentomatoes.com/tv/the_simpsons/s08 | title=The Simpsons | website=[[Rotten Tomatoes]] }}</ref>

