|WrittenBy=Ron Hauge
|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1997|4|13}}
|ProdCode=4F16
|ShortSummary=Bart gets a credit card and buys a well trained new dog called Laddie. When Bart could not pay the balance on the credit card the bank repossesses Laddie. Instead of giving them Laddie, Bart gives the repo men [[Santa's Little Helper]]. Feeling guilty, Bart gives Laddie to the police and sets out to find Santa's Little Helper and finds him at a blind man's house. Bart tries to kidnap his dog, but instead the blind man alerts the police. When they arrive, Laddie, who is now a police dog, sniffs out a bag of marijuana and the blind man gets arrested. Bart can then leave with [[Santa's Little Helper]].{{sfn|Richmond & Coffman|1997 |p=233}}
|NoViewersOnMainList=y|Viewers=13.25<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/article/the-los-angeles-times/41386061/|title=National Nielsen Viewership (April 7-13, 1997)|date=April 16, 1997|access-date=March 2, 2023|work=[[The Los Angeles Times]]|via=[[Newspapers.com]]}}{{free access}}</ref><hr>7.9<ref>{{#invoke:cite|news|title=ABC ratings take a record nose dive |work=Sun-Sentinel |agency=Associated Press |page=4E |date=April 17, 1997}}</ref><br><small>(HH){{efn|name=HH|(HH) denotes that the numbers listed are the number of households the episode was viewed in.}}</small>
