|WrittenBy=[[Donick Cary]]
|OriginalAirDate={{Start date|1997|4|27}}
|ProdCode=4F18
|ShortSummary=Marge is concerned that [[Reverend Lovejoy]] does not meet the needs of his parishioners and becomes the new advice giver at the Church. When Marge gains a loyal following, Lovejoy gets concerned that he has become "shepherd without a flock". Meanwhile, Homer finds an old Japanese product, "Mr. Sparkle", a dish-washing detergent, with a logo that oddly resembles him. When he calls up the company behind the product, he finds Mr. Sparkle is a composite of two company logos. Marge is unable to help Ned Flanders in a crisis and calls up Lovejoy for help. Lovejoy solves the crisis and gets his congregants' interest in his next sermon telling the story.{{sfn|Richmond & Coffman|1997 |p=235}}
